  ```

  ### Checklist fields

  | Field | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | `group_id` | Group ID from the path. |
  | `viewer_member_id` | Caller's membership ID in this group. Compare with `assigned_to.member_id` to display "you". |
  | `is_frozen` | True in SETTLING and CLOSED, when all item action flags are false. |
  | `filter` | Applied item filter. |
  | `summary` | Overall checklist totals. The filter and page change only the item list and pagination. |
  | `member_claims` | Active group memberships in ascending member ID order, including memberships with zero claims. Each contains the member fields and `claimed_item_count`. |
  | `items` | Current page in descending item ID order, excluding soft-deleted items. |
  | `pagination` | `page`, `limit` and `total`, the number of items matching the filter before pagination. |

  ### Summary fields

  | Field | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | `total_items` | Group items plus personal reminders. |
  | `group_item_count` | All GROUP items, the progress denominator. |
  | `personal_item_count` | All PERSONAL reminders. |
  | `claimed_item_count` | GROUP items currently assigned, the progress numerator. |
  | `unclaimed_item_count` | GROUP items without an assignee. |
  | `my_claimed_item_count` | GROUP items assigned to the caller. |
  | `progress_percent` | Claimed GROUP items divided by all GROUP items, multiplied by 100 and rounded to the nearest integer. Zero when there are no GROUP items. |

  With the sample data, `filter=mine` returns only item 10 and `pagination.total` is 1. `summary.total_items` stays 4. An empty list or out-of-range page returns 200 with `items: []`. A whole checklist with no items has zero counts and an active-members report showing zero claims.

  ### Item fields

  Create, Claim and Release return the same item shape in `data`.

  | Field | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | `id` | Checklist item ID used for Claim, Release and Delete. |
  | `title` | Saved title after trimming. A title can be repeated. |
  | `type` | `GROUP` or `PERSONAL`. |
  | `created_by` | Member who added the item. Render when the creator toggle is on. |
  | `assigned_to` | Current assignee, or `null` for an available item or personal reminder. |
  | `can_claim` | True for an available GROUP item in an ACTIVE group. |
  | `can_release` | True for the caller's own claim in an ACTIVE group. |
  | `can_delete` | True in an ACTIVE group for an available item, personal reminder, or a claimed item when the caller owns the group. |
  | `created_at` | Time the item was added. |
  | `updated_at` | Creation time or time of the latest claim, release or automatic release. Reads and retries that keep the current state preserve it. |

  Member objects include `member_id`, `user_id`, `name` and `avatar_url`. An avatar URL is signed and temporary. Missing or inaccessible avatars and storage signing failures yield `null`. Timestamps are RFC 3339 strings and can include a timezone offset.

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Invalid group ID, unsupported filter, invalid page/limit, or an overflowing page offset. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | The Authorization header is missing or does not have the Bearer token format. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | The token is invalid, is a refresh token, or has an invalid user ID. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | The access token expired. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | The access token was revoked. |
  | 403 | `CHECKLIST_FORBIDDEN` | `only active group members can access the checklist` | The caller has no active membership in this group. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | The caller's membership is active and their account is inactive. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | An active membership exists but its user is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 404 | `GROUP_NOT_FOUND` | `group not found` | The group is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | The database, transaction or token blacklist lookup failed. |

  **Example 403**

  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "code": "CHECKLIST_FORBIDDEN",
    "error": "only active group members can access the checklist"
  }
  ```
}
